{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Envelope Propagation Simulation\n",
    "### SET Resonance Substrate Model\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates **resonance envelope propagation** in the SET substrate.\n",
    "\n",
    "Objectives:\n",
    "- initialize two localized resonance sources\n",
    "- evolve SET fields using the substrate solver\n",
    "- observe envelope formation, propagation, and interference\n",
    "- visualize envelope masks and overlays\n",
    "- compute envelope propagation metrics\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "from simulations.core.substrate_solver import (\n",
    "    Grid, SubstrateParams, SubstrateState, step\n",
    ")\n",
    "from docs.resonance_substrate_model.tools.visualization.field_plotter import (\n",
    "    plot_spin, plot_charge, plot_temperature\n",
    ")\n",
    "from docs.resonance_substrate_model.tools.visualization.envelope_viewer import (\n",
    "    compute_envelope, envelope_mask, visualize_envelope\n",
    ")\n",
    "from docs.resonance_substrate_model.tools.visualization.triadic_space_mapper import (\n",
    "    visualize_triadic_state\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Simulation Parameters\n",
    "Define grid, time step, and substrate parameters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "nx, ny = 160, 160\n",
    "dx = dy = 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "grid = Grid(nx=nx, ny=ny, dx=dx, dy=dy)\n",
    "\n",
    "params = SubstrateParams(\n",
    "    D_S=1.0, D_C=1.0, D_T=1.0,\n",
    "    gamma_S=0.05, gamma_C=0.05, gamma_T=0.05,\n",
    "    lambda_SC=1.0,\n",
    "    lambda_ST=0.6,\n",
    "    beta_CS=0.4,\n",
    "    eta_S=0.1, eta_C=0.1,\n",
    "    T0=0.0\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "dt = 0.01\n",
    "steps = 2500"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Initialize Two Resonant Sources\n",
    "We create two Gaussian Charge sources that will generate two resonance envelopes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Spin is initialized with small random perturbations.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "state = SubstrateState(grid)\n",
    "\n",
    "x = np.linspace(-1, 1, nx)\n",
    "y = np.linspace(-1, 1, ny)\n",
    "X, Y = np.meshgrid(x, y, indexing=\"ij\")\n",
    "\n    ",
    "# Two Gaussian Charge sources\n",
    "sigma = 0.15\n",
    "C1 = np.exp(-(((X + 0.4)**2 + Y**2) / (2 * sigma**2)))\n",
    "C2 = np.exp(-(((X - 0.4)**2 + Y**2) / (2 * sigma**2)))\n",
    "\n",
    "state.C = C1 + C2\n",
    "\n",
    "# Small random Spin field\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(123)\n",
    "state.S = rng.normal(scale=0.1, size=(nx, ny, 3))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Uniform Temperature\n",
    "state.T[:, :] = 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_charge(state.C, title=\"Initial Charge Field (Two Sources)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Run Simulation\n",
    "Store snapshots for envelope visualization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "snapshots = []\n",
    "snapshot_interval = 250\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(steps):\n",
    "    step(state, params, dt)\n",
    "    if i % snapshot_interval == 0:\n",
    "        snapshots.append((i, state.S.copy(), state.C.copy(), state.T.copy()))\n",
    "        print(f\"Step {i}/{steps}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Envelope Field Evolution\n",
    "Visualize the envelope field R(x,y) over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(snapshots), figsize=(4*len(snapshots), 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, (i, S, C, T) in zip(axes, snapshots):\n",
    "    R = compute_envelope(S, C, T, alpha=1.0, theta=0.1, dx=grid.dx, dy=grid.dy)\n",
    "    im = ax.imshow(R.T, origin='lower', cmap='coolwarm')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Step {i}\")\n",
    "    plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Envelope Mask Evolution\n",
    "Binary mask showing where resonance conditions are satisfied."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(snapshots), figsize=(4*len(snapshots), 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, (i, S, C, T) in zip(axes, snapshots):\n",
    "    R = compute_envelope(S, C, T, alpha=1.0, theta=0.1, dx=grid.dx, dy=grid.dy)\n",
    "    mask = envelope_mask(R)\n",
    "    ax.imshow(mask.T, origin='lower', cmap='gray_r')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Step {i}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Final Triadic Overlay\n",
    "Shows the combined SET field structure at the end of the simulation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "visualize_triadic_state(state, grid, prefix=\"Final Envelope State\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Envelope Propagation Metric\n",
    "We compute the **total envelope area** over time:\n",
    "\n",
    "\

\[ A(t) = \\sum R(x,y) > 0 \\]

"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def envelope_area(S, C, T, grid):\n",
    "    R = compute_envelope(S, C, T, alpha=1.0, theta=0.1, dx=grid.dx, dy=grid.dy)\n",
    "    return np.sum(R > 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "state2 = SubstrateState(grid)\n",
    "state2.C = C1 + C2\n",
    "state2.S = rng.normal(scale=0.1, size=(nx, ny, 3))\n",
    "\n",
    "areas = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for i in range(steps):\n",
    "    step(state2, params, dt)\n",
    "    areas.append(envelope_area(state2.S, state2.C, state2.T, grid))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(areas)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Envelope Area vs Time\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Step\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Envelope Area\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
